{
  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_inputs",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1068
        },
        "text": "World normal, view direction and tangent, mesh UV and the light direction (normalised once)."
      },
      {
        "color": "#f472b6",
        "id": "note_sheen",
        "position": {
          "x": 1294,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2072
        },
        "text": "Velvet fibres stand up and scatter light sideways, so the cloth is brightest where `N·V` is small: `sheen = (1 − N·V)^power`. A half-Lambert term `½·N·L + ½` (weighted `0.35 + 0.65·wrap`) keeps the unlit side from glowing as much."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_aniso",
        "position": {
          "x": 1294,
          "y": 571
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 1460
        },
        "text": "The shared **Anisotropic Highlight** kit returns a Kajiya–Kay streak along the tangent. `streak = lerp(1, 0.25 + saturate(spec), anisotropy)` modulates the sheen: with Anisotropy 0 nothing changes, at 1 the sheen collapses into tangent-aligned bands (satin, brushed silk)."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_emit",
        "position": {
          "x": 3570,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 848
        },
        "text": "`emission = sheenColor × sheen × streak × intensity` — added as emissive so it works on every target."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_weave",
        "position": {
          "x": 3570,
          "y": 559
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1766
        },
        "text": "A checker at *Weave Scale* threads per UV unit: `weave = lerp(1, checker, amount)`. `darken = 1 − faceDarken × (N·V)²`. Albedo = fabric × weave × darken."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 5540,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "Albedo, low smoothness and the sheen as emission."
      }
    ],
